I think prior to answering the question of "should stashes be counted as
loot when you die, and how", it might be better to properly reform the
scoring system so that the value of objects had a significant impact.

For example, I routinely drop the Book next to the stairs in the
Sanctum.  I leave the Bell there too if I have plenty of
portal-detectery and /oSDD.  And I ditch the Candelabrum if I have
either the Eyes or a magic lamp since I won't need superior light on
Astral later for jumping.

Partly I do this because my only actual goal is ascension; partly I do
this because the points for these objects are totally meaningless.  When
a relatively low-score, no-trickery ascension (ie. not a pacifist, not a
speedrun) is 1.87 million, the 12.5k* for these artifacts just isn't
significant.

